`const insert = `${prefix}${fence}
${selected}
${fence}
`;` — when the selection ends at a line start (a whole-line selection such as "one
"), `selected` already ends in a newline, so an extra empty line lands inside the fence. Likewise, if `selected` itself contains a ``` line, the opening fence is closed early and the remainder leaks out as markdown/HTML text; no longer-fence widening (````) is attempted.
